<title>GERMANY: Global One declines comment on C&amp;W rumours.</title>
<headline>Global One declines comment on C&amp;W rumours.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of Global One, the joint venture of Deutsche Telekom, France Telecom and Sprint Corp, declined to comment on speculation the company was in talks with Cable and Wireless.</p>
<p>&quot;No comment,&quot; Viesturs Vucins told reporters in Munich when asked about press reports that Cable and Wireless was interested in joining the three-way telecommunications alliance.</p>
<p>Cable and Wireless is expected to bail out of its current alliance with German utilities Veba AG and RWE AG. It is widely believed that Cable and Wireless and Global One have held talks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
